Sync-instr + pinned-output rescue (mm20/mm23).

mm20: every stream sync timed cumulatively, exported as
ggml_backend_cuda_sync_stats through the backend proc registry (dlopened
modules are RTLD_LOCAL - dlsym cannot see them). Fleet verdict: 0.18
ms/token total sync wait - the CC sync tax does not exist.

mm23: cudaMallocHost fails inside CVM tenant environments (suspect: the
MPS pinned-device limit in the tenant env), and ggml's silent pageable
fallback makes the logits extraction a BLOCKING full-stream wait
(out_get = 14.20 of the fleet's 15.6 ms/token). Before surrendering to a
pageable buffer, pin malloc'd pages via cudaHostRegister - a different
driver path. Local proof under GGML_CUDA_NO_PINNED=1: register succeeds,
buffer reports CUDA_Host, out_get 0. If it also succeeds on the fleet,
the blocking wait becomes an async submit and 1-4 ms/token comes back on
every decode mode.

